    <name>🌊 LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-08-25T12:00:00Z (newest of 3-day mosaic)<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (ERDDAP)<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-22 03:16 UTC<br/><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE (daily composite)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_clarity/legend.png?v=2026-09-22_0316_UTC" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Diffuse attenuation coefficient for PAR (m^-1), continuous: <b>LOWEST 0.022</b> clearest (dark blue) → common 0.165 → <b>HIGHEST+ 6.34</b> most turbid (deep purple). Larger values always mean murkier water; source values are never altered.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP VIIRS Kd(PAR) diffuse attenuation, Near Real-Time, Global 4 km, Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNkdparDaily)<br/><a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNkdparDaily.html">https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNkdparDaily.html</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</h2><p>Diffuse attenuation coefficient for photosynthetically available radiation (KdPAR): how quickly sunlight fades with depth. Larger values mean more turbid water; smaller values mean clearer water. Source values are never altered for color convenience.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_clarity/legend.png?v=2026-09-22_0316_UTC" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Diffuse attenuation coefficient for PAR (m^-1), continuous: <b>LOWEST 0.022</b> clearest (dark blue) → common 0.165 → <b>HIGHEST+ 6.34</b> most turbid (deep purple). Larger values always mean murkier water; source values are never altered.</p><p><b>Exact variable:</b> kd_par (Diffuse Attenuation Coefficient for PAR; NOAA MECB algorithm; product status Experimental)<br/><b>Units:</b> m^-1<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP VIIRS Kd(PAR) diffuse attenuation, Near Real-Time, Global 4 km, Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNkdparDaily)<br/><b>Update:</b> daily composites<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-08-25T12:00:00Z (mosaic 2026-08-25..2026-08-23)<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-22 03:16 UTC<br/><b>Why turbid water turns red/purple:</b> Rare very-turbid water (storm resuspension, river plumes, intense blooms) compresses into red-violet/deep-purple; ordinary clear conditions own most of the color resolution.<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNkdparDaily.html">ERDDAP dataset</a></p>]]></description>
